{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak now, please, in the ears of the people, and let them ask, etc.</b> The Sages said (Berakhot 9a) that נָא means nothing other than the language of a request — so that that righteous man should not say, '״וַעֲבָדוּם וְעִנּוּ אוֹתָם״ He fulfilled in them, but ״וְאַחֲרֵי כֵן יֵצְאוּ בִּרְכוּשׁ גָּדוֹל״ He did not fulfill in them.' And the question is: why did the fulfillment of His promise depend on the word of that righteous man? Without his word, would HaShem not fulfill His word, heaven forbid? And it appears that this may be resolved according to what is concluded in tractate Berakhot (there), that ״וַיַּשְׁאִלוּם״ — Israel did against their will, because of the burden of the road. According to this, HaShem fulfilled the terms of His promise when He showed them the place in which the promise would be fulfilled; and what more is there for Him to do if they themselves do not wish to receive? Nevertheless there is reason to fear that that righteous man might say, etc., for he would not know that they did not ask to receive, and since Abraham was righteous and upright, it would be a trouble in his eyes that they were enslaved for nothing. And therefore it was said to him ״וְאַחֲרֵי כֵן יֵצְאוּ בִּרְכוּשׁ גָּדוֹל״. In the word ״וְאַחֲרֵי כֵן״ He indicated that they would take for themselves the wages of their labor from the Egyptians, and therefore He used ״וְאַחֲרֵי כֵן״, for wages are not paid except at the end. And even though there is no hindrance to HaShem to give Israel great wealth without their needing to take from the Egyptians by way of request and subterfuge, nevertheless the El of justice did so to rescue from their hands the wages of their labor, as is found in chapter Chelek (Sanhedrin 91a) in the case of Geviha ben Pesisa, etc. And therefore the mind of that righteous man would not be satisfied with any wealth except the wealth of Egypt in exchange for their labor, for through this he would receive consolation for the hard labor with which his seed was worked. And this is what it says: ״וְאַחֲרֵי כֵן יֵצְאוּ בִּרְכוּשׁ גָּדוֹל״ — He did not fulfill in them. Rashi brought the expression ״וְאַחֲרֵי כֵן״ for the reason that we have mentioned."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:19:26.122592352Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}